WEBVTT

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:11.080
Please don't expect too much from it.
This story is a simple illustration of the three
Minami sisters and the ordinary life they lead.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.260
Put your winter clothes in that box.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.200
Okay.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.350
And put the clothes you
don't want in that other box.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.410
Okay.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.080
Kana, do you want this?

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.140
I'm too big for it now.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.670
It fits perfectly!

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.870
That's great.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.450
That reminds me,

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.660
the pool's opening up soon, isn't it?

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.430
Yes.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.050
That's right.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.640
I wouldn't say I dislike
.the pool in particular,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.130
but I don't think the pool likes me.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.440
Well, I have some good news for you.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.970
That's...

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:48.940
No way...

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:49.250
Haruka

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.570
It's Haruka-neesama's!
Haruka

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:50.690
Haruka
It's Haruka-neesama's!

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.400
That's right.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.690
Hey! Kana!

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.510
Back when Haruka was in middle school,

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:57.850
she swam underwater for about
50 meters in this swimsuit.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.580
You know what that means, right?

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.580
I could swim without needing to breathe!

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.080
Hey!

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.170
I owe you one, Kana.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.710
I still don't know how to take breaths in the
water, but with this, even I can swim!

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:13.010
Let's head out to the Pacific
Ocean later for a dip.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:17.890
It looks kind of...

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:18.970
baggy.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:19.890
Of course it is!

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:24.550
Well, I'm sure you'll learn how to
swim by the time you fit into it.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:25.140
Hopefully.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:29.980
You got my hopes up for nothing, you moron!

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.950
Making Chilled Noodles

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:11.460
Apparently the Chinese restaurant a block
away started selling chilled noodles.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.000
Oh, the place we went to last year?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.210
It was pretty good.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.370
All right, let's do it!

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:17.860
Summer begins early for us!

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.630
Yeah.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.080
Akira.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.800
Oh, hello, Kana-san.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.620
What would you say to some
chilled noodles after school?

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.310
Let's start our summer early!

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.680
Sounds good.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.530
You're still in your winter uniform?

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:33.620
Yeah.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:34.970
It's still kind of chilly sometimes,

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.020
so we haven't all switched over yet.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:39.860
Akira, you're not ready for chilled noodles.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.550
Eating summer food like that in your
winter uniform is just disrespectful.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.640
I never realized chilled noodle
etiquette was so unforgiving.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:45.660
When you get rid of that uniform, talk to me.
I never realized chilled noodle
etiquette was so unforgiving.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.550
When you get rid of that uniform, talk to me.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.450
Sure.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:50.020
That's too bad.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:53.000
I would've loved for you to join us.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.020
Really?

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.670
You mean you'd love... me...

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:59.110
That Chinese restaurant is really good.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:02.130
But I'd feel a bit embarrassed going
there with another girl on our own.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.640
I see.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.450
You'd feel more at ease
.with a guy there. Any guy.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:06.970
Seconds!

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.600
See you.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.720
Later.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.370
What were you and Minami chatting about?

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:17.650
F-Fujioka-san!

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:19.800
H-He's gonna kick me...

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:23.650
If I let anything slip, he'll
...definitely kick me in the leg...

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.660
This guy's...

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:28.950
the ball-kicking Badass!

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.260
You'll tell me the truth, right?

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.430
W-Well, she almost invited
.me for chilled noodles.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.460
Chi-Chilled noodles?!

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.730
Man, I'm jealous.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.260
I wish I could be there,
eating those noodles.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.310
Does he like chilled noodles?

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:45.530
But I'm not very "summery" right now,
so she didn't invite me.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:46.750
You're not "summery"?

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.770
So if you are, she'll invite you?

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:50.000
I guess so.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.500
Apparently, it's important to wear
clothes that fit the season.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.300
I see.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.620
I'm glad I wore a shirt underneath.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.410
Freshman,

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.480
what was your name?

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.240
Akira!

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.640
Akira.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.500
Thank you for telling me that.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.000
Bye.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.660
Fujioka-san...

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.750
Hang on a second.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.860
Just wearing a button-down
shirt isn't summery enough.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:24.880
You can't simply leave it
buttoned all the way up.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:29.070
You need to unbutton the collar,
untuck it, and look like you're cooling off.

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:29.930
I see.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.680
And since it's hot out,

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.800
you need to act all worn out from the heat.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:35.940
I see.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.270
Akira.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.310
Thank you for telling me that.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:40.950
See you later.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:45.820
I hope you'll get to eat those
chilled noodles, Fujioka.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.070
Fujioka-kun?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.550
A rare side of Fujioka-kun!

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:03.590
Fujioka-kun?!

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.470
Sh-She didn't invite me?

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.100
Did he become a delinquent?

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.230
She hasn't invited me yet.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:27.510
Maybe you need to make it
clearer that you're hot.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:28.610
I see.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:35.240
Is Fujioka-kun trying to
pick a fight with Akira?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.330
Fujioka-kun...

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.500
Man, it's hot.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.730
A rare side of Fujioka-kun!

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:47.670
Fujioka-kun!

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:49.680
It's so hot.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:51.590
She's still not inviting me...

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.680
Fujioka-kun <i>did</i> become a delinquent!

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.060
She hasn't invited me yet.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:02.060
Maybe you need to make it
.even clearer that you're hot.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.280
Fujioka's totally picking a fight with Akira!

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.610
Fujioka-kun...

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.790
Damn, it's hot...

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.910
Really damn hot.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.450
A rare side of Fujioka-kun!

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.080
So hot.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.330
So friggin' hot.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.670
She's not even thinking about it!

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.460
Fujioka became a total delinquent!

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.880
Are you sure this will work?

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.220
I think it should, but...

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:34.510
Fujioka's beating the crap out of Akira!

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.420
Fujioka-kun...

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.560
What am I doing wrong?

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:42.480
Fujioka-kun.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.330
Do you have a minute?

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.550
What is it?

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:47.400
Sorry if I got the wrong idea.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:52.500
But if you wanted to have chilled noodles that
badly, maybe I could ask Kana to invite you?

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.120
What?!

00:07:56.570 --> 00:07:59.280
Maybe he's just feeling stressed.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:01.200
Please!

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.120
It's fine.

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:09.880
The model student set that delinquent straight!

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.960
This is what school life is all about!

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:14.910
'Sup!

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:15.750
Minami!

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:16.940
Hey, Kana.

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:19.640
Fujioka, you must be stressed out.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:23.420
There's nothing like chilled noodles
to help you unwind, you know.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:24.970
Um, Kana, do you—

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:25.960
What?!

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:32.910
I see.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:34.820
So that's it.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:37.290
I finally found the right answer.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:41.950
Good morning.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.920
Kana, you're finally up.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.440
Oh, Chiaki.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:46.400
Where's Haruka?

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:49.130
She had to leave early this morning.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.740
She left me in charge of breakfast.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:54.620
My special menu for this morning:

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:58.620
A bacon toast pizza with
extra cheese and potato chips.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:00.260
Don't mind if I do!

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:01.570
You moron!

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:03.930
That was <i>my</i> special menu.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.530
Does it matter which one of us eats first?

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:08.300
I mean, you made enough
for the both of us, right?

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:10.070
Fine.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:14.260
This is good! It's really good, Chiaki!

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:17.150
I just woke up, so my body is
absorbing all the grease!

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.450
I see.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.480
That was great.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:21.200
I see.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.360
Now for a nap.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:24.460
Already?

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:32.210
Maybe I'll go with this.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.350
What about you, Maki?

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:34.300
What?

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.390
That one comes in two pieces.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:40.050
Isn't this pretty standard?

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:47.680
The left and right cups are just
held together by a thread?!

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:48.810
What? What is it?

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.180
Which one should I get?

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.430
All done.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.260
My special lunch menu:

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.970
Yesterday's leftover beef curry
with a buttered potato.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.330
Don't mind if I do!

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:08.460
H-Hey.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.930
This is good! It's really good, Chiaki!

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:15.260
I can feel the carbohydrates
dancing in my stomach!

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.220
I see.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.240
Now for a nap.

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:19.090
Again?

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:22.540
When should we hit the beach?

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:26.250
Sorry, but I have to go alone.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:31.440
It's calling to me. A summer adventure.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.350
Can Kana and the others tag along?

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.460
Of course. The more the merrier.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:36.240
Hey!

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.440
Don't ignore me!

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:40.570
It's ready.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.280
My after-lunch special menu:

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.580
Gum syrup cola!

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:47.460
Here.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.650
Thanks.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.510
Here.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:58.470
Thanks.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:00.920
Here.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.180
Thanks.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:10.730
All right, I have to go buy food for dinner.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:11.530
See ya.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:12.570
Bye.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.070
Th-This is...

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:25.330
Chiaki.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.660
Thanks to your great menu,

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.750
I've gained great weight!

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.460
What are you going to do about this?!

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:33.590
You've gained weight?

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:34.550
I'm not surprised.

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:35.710
Wh-What?

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.080
They were special meals, enriched with fat.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:42.580
I had prepared a normal menu for you
as well, but you helped yourself to mine.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:44.710
Wh-Why would you do that?

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:46.350
Because I came to a realization.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:46.850
<i>What</i> realization?

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:51.230
If I stored fats in my body over the summer,
I'd be able to float more easily in water!

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:53.730
In other words, it would help me swim!

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:05.710
In your carelessness, you forgot
something very important.

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:06.330
What?

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:10.000
Indeed, adding more body fat
will increase your buoyancy,

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.910
but what of your ability to tread water?

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.170
Muscle!

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.960
I'm home!

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.970
Sorry I'm so late.

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.910
I'll make dinner right away.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.430
No, Haruka.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:27.230
Tonight's menu is already set in stone.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.770
Our special menu for tonight is...

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:31.810
A thousand hops of jump rope and no dinner!

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.930
Let's go, Chiaki!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:33.940
Yeah!

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:37.610
Huh?

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:38.980
Let's go!

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:39.610
Yeah!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.110
One!

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:42.000
Ow!

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.330
Get up, Chiaki!

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.110
One more time!

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.280
Y-Yeah.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:46.970
One!

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:47.890
Ow!

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:50.670
How about some sit-ups?

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.650
How about a jog?

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:15.550
Uchida, what are you doing?

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:17.750
I'm making my summer vacation schedule.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.110
That's good to see. Lemme take a look.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.360
What should I do?

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:27.560
Should I draw in one more star?

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.240
There we go.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:30.220
Ow!

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:32.240
What's this schedule supposed to be?

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.130
It's a work in progress!

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:37.930
Think about what you'll be doing during
the day before you put effort into sleep.

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:39.770
What are you drawing stars in for?

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:41.640
I'm thinking about it seriously!

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:42.670
Don't bother me!

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:46.000
But you know, even if you
<i>do</i> make plans for summer,

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.440
they never seem to work out anyway.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:49.910
Just draw up your ideal plan.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:51.400
You sound unusually serious.

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:52.280
Oh, I see.

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:53.180
My ideal plan.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:54.310
That reminds me.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:57.880
When Kana was in elementary
school, she stuck to her plan exactly.

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.310
Huh? Kana-chan did?

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:00.280
Yeah.

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:01.820
She threw a dart at it and hit "sleep."

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:02.910
Study
Play
Relax
Snack
Sleep

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:03.650
Yay!

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:06.770
So she slept.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.410
That's not a plan!

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:11.200
Akira, today's the last day of term.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.370
Yes, it is.

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:17.210
It's hard to see people in your class
once summer vacation starts.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.510
What should I do?

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:21.000
Who do you want to see? Is it a girl?

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.310
Never mind! I'm sorry!

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:25.170
I didn't mean to pry too deep.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:28.430
I think the most important
.thing is to stay in touch.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.350
S-Stay in touch?

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:31.420
What do you mean?

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:35.470
Let's say you go to a family restaurant after
.school today with a few of your classmates.

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:37.180
A family restaurant?

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:38.130
While you're there, you can make plans
.for a shopping trip in the next town over.

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:40.230
Hey, let's go shopping in the next town over!

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:40.620
While you're there, you can make plans
.for a shopping trip in the next town over.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.080
Their chilled noodles are so good!

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.230
Shopping?

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:48.240
And when you go shopping
and look at swimsuits and yukata,

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.240
you'll naturally end up making plans
to go to the beach and a fireworks show together.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.000
What do you think of this one, Fujioka?

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:51.370
I love it!
you'll naturally end up making plans
to go to the beach and a fireworks show together.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.190
I love it!

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:52.530
What do you think of this one?

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:53.710
Fireworks?!
What do you think of this one?

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:54.870
I love it.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:58.880
And when you get back from the beach
and the fireworks, summer vacation will be over,

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:01.410
and you'll see each other the
next day at the opening ceremony.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:03.480
They're beautiful.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:04.330
Yes, they are.

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:04.350
They're beautiful.
Yes, they are.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:05.020
They're beautiful.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:05.590
Yes, they are.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:09.150
Anyway, you just need to keep making plans!

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:11.580
I-It's the perfect strategy!

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:15.140
We'll end the summer with a fireworks show!

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.390
But to make that happen, we'll need
to go to a family restaurant together!

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:20.080
Is there anything we're missing?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.310
What about karaoke?

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:22.130
Studying at the lib—

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:22.690
No.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:24.940
H-Hey, Minami.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.260
Hey, perfect timing.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:28.500
You want to come too?

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:29.030
Huh?

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:30.400
Wh-Where?

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.320
We're going to decide right now.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:36.120
We made a "Today's Plans" board.

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:42.160
We'll drop an eraser on it, and
whatever it lands on is what we'll do.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.380
I see.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.130
Family restaurant zone.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:52.400
I'll do it.

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:53.800
All right.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:02.260
A rare side of Fujioka-kun!

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:03.150
Fujioka-kun...

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:14.030
Get the family restaurant,
get the beach and fireworks.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:15.490
Family restaurant!

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:26.000
Barbecue

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:34.090
Family restaurant!

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:35.090
Yes!

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.350
No!

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.350
Go back!

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.620
Huh? A family restaurant?

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.400
That's kind of plain.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:54.450
Yeah.

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:59.010
Yes!

00:16:59.010 --> 00:16:59.910
Huh?
Yes!

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:02.910
Fujioka-kun looks really happy.
Yes!

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.620
I guess he just really likes family restaurants?
Yes!

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.290
Family restaurant!

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:11.300
There were a bunch more
...interesting things on there too...

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:12.550
Family Restaurant Hour
Ramen rice

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:19.520
Fireworks, the beach, even a sleepover...

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:25.660
Maybe he didn't want to
come to <i>this</i> family restaurant?

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:30.770
Huh?

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:33.650
My dad got us a bunch of fireworks.

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:36.350
But there's way too many for just our family,

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:37.570
so we're sharing them with everyone.

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.240
Wow! Wow!

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.660
There's a ton in here!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.350
All right! Let's light them today!

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.820
Let's call everyone over!

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:44.850
Yeah!

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:56.060
Hello?

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:58.800
Oh, thank you for calling.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:03.220
Huh? You went to a family restaurant,
but you didn't make plans to meet again?

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:05.070
What were you thinking?

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.840
Sorry. That was rude of me.

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:08.440
Sweet! There's one more!

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:08.980
What the heck?!

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:09.150
But then you suddenly got
invited to fireworks today?

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:10.670
You're not cleaning the cob properly.

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:11.630
You have no right to this ear.

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:12.980
Good job!
You have no right to this ear.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:13.500
Come on! Corn tastes better
when you eat it this way!

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:14.790
Listen closely.

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:17.260
You won't get anywhere if you're
.satisfied just hanging out with them.

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:17.460
I will not accept such an opinion!

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:19.040
You need a new goal.
I will not accept such an opinion!

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:19.370
Apologize to the corn!
You need a new goal.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:20.440
What would be a good goal, assuming the
person you're talking about is a girl?
Apologize to the corn!

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:21.960
What about you, Natsuki—
What would be a good goal, assuming the
person you're talking about is a girl?

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:25.000
How the heck do you eat them that cleanly?!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.750
Huh? You want to hold her hand?

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.000
Yeah! That's a good start!

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:31.950
Okay. Good-bye.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.040
Who was that from, Akira?

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.220
You got pretty worked up.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.260
A scary upperclassman at school.

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:43.260
I get the feeling he can't
survive without me, though.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.820
Sounds pretty complicated.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:47.330
I know just what you're talking about.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:49.020
You do, Natsuki?

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:52.350
I'd better get going.

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:54.340
Don't cause them trouble, now.

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:57.410
Good luck, Fujioka-san.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.040
There we go. It's lit.

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:04.030
All right, let's do this!

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:07.170
You're lighting the rocket, okay, Fujioka?

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.710
O-Okay.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:18.090
Wait... Did I turn off the stove?

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.940
Um... I'm going back home for a minute.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:30.640
Huh? The candle went out.

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:33.710
Huh? Where's the person with the lighter?

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:35.800
She had to go back home for a minute.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:37.660
Oh, come on!

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:39.840
Now we can't light these things!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.330
Anyone here have a lighter?

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:44.370
I don't.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.730
I don't think any of us would.

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:48.130
We're in elementary school, after all.

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:49.700
Oh well.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:51.090
Here.

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:52.200
What's that for?

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.170
This is...

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.820
No way!

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:58.170
Huh? Oh well.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:58.800
Then...

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:00.650
Wh-What?

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:01.510
This is...

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:03.800
No way!

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:06.010
Huh? Again?

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:06.920
Then...

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:07.530
Huh?

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:08.560
This is...

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:11.340
No way!

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.080
I'm out of options!

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:19.360
If you thought to bring all this stuff,
why not bring a match or a lighter?!

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:21.110
All right.

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:25.700
But I need to think up a way to
hold her hand before I get to the park.

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:30.300
No... I can't think of anything good this time.

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:34.790
If I don't think of something quick,
I'll arrive at the park with nothing!

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:39.800
Hurry! Think!

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.550
Minami.

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.930
We didn't have a light, right? I got one.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:46.180
I'm already there!

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.090
Crap! I need to think of <i>something</i>!

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:49.840
Oh, thanks a ton.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:51.180
I'll pay you back.

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:52.570
No, it's okay.

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.850
But it's our fault.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:56.110
Seriously, it's okay.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:57.640
No, no, no. Just take it.

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:58.660
It's okay!

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:01.230
I'm telling you to take it!

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:05.080
All right! What should we do first?

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:06.210
A rocket!

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:06.650
A black snake!

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:07.660
A spinner!
A black snake!

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.110
Let's start with smoke bombs. Come on.

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:11.880
Hey, Fujioka, want to—

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:15.360
Hell yeah!

00:21:15.360 --> 00:21:17.670
I've never seen someone so happy over 100 yen.
Hell yeah!

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:28.430
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.430
You held her hand?

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.220
Congratulations!

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:33.760
What about the next—

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:37.220
You didn't make plans to meet again?

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:39.380
What were you thinking?

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:42.060
Sorry. That was rude of me.

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:43.030
I'm home!

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.030
Hell yeah!

00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:24.840
I wonder if Fujioka-kun's going
anywhere over summer vacation.

00:23:24.840 --> 00:23:27.350
What? I might get to see him
if I go to a family restaurant?

00:23:27.350 --> 00:23:30.550
Next time: "A Girl Cannot Hide
Her Suntan, Nor Her Heart."

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:34.100
Riko, one of these days, you should have a
proper conversation with Fujioka-kun for once.
